            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cellular networks have been the focus of studies in modern systems biology. They are crucial in understanding cell functions and related diseases. We review some past progress in both the theory and experiments, and we also provide several future perspectives for the field.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
